# Line endings
#
# The repository was 121 CRLF files against 62 LF before this existed, because
# it has only ever been committed from Windows with core.autocrlf=true. That is
# invisible until a second platform touches it, at which point contributors get
# whole-file diffs on files they did not edit.
#
# `text=auto` normalises to LF in the repository; `eol=lf` checks out LF in the
# working tree too, so every platform sees the same bytes. Nothing here needs
# CRLF — there are no .bat, .cmd or .ps1 files, and Node, Vite and Playwright
# are all indifferent.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary — never normalise these. The visual regression baselines in
# test/visual/*-snapshots/ are the reason this matters: a single byte of
# "normalisation" would corrupt 30 reference screenshots and fail every visual
# test at once.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.eot binary

# Committed for reproducible installs, but a lockfile diff is never read by a
# human. `-diff` collapses it to "Binary files differ" in review.
package-lock.json -diff

# Language statistics should describe the library, not its examples. Without
# this, 40 HTML example pages compete with 127 TypeScript sources and GitHub
# labels the repository HTML.
examples/** linguist-documentation
